<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qal'at al-Bahrain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bahrain Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qal'at al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> is an archaeological site on the north coast of Bahrain, occupied from about 2300 BCE to the 18th century. It was a walled town and probably the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a>, and later the site of a fort rebuilt by the Portuguese in the 16th century. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qalat-al-bahrain.jpg" alt="Qal'at al-Bahrain" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Falbisoner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bahrain_Fort_March_2015.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
